From: JohnTheFarm3r <104281500+JohnTheFarm3r@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: device_enumerator_udev: Add devices once access
 is granted

A media device that cannot be opened when it is added, for instance
because the seat has not granted the session access to it yet, was
recorded as seen and never tried again. When the active session of a
seat changes, its devices get a "change" event once their permissions
are updated. Forget devices that could not be opened and add them on a
later "change" event, so cameras appear once access is granted.

Signed-off-by: JohnTheFarm3r <104281500+JohnTheFarm3r@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/src/libcamera/device_enumerator_udev.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/device_enumerator_udev.cpp
@@ -92,8 +92,15 @@
 	if (!strcmp(subsystem, "media")) {
 		std::unique_ptr<MediaDevice> media =
 			createDevice(udev_device_get_devnode(dev));
-		if (!media)
+		if (!media) {
+			/*
+			 * The device could not be opened, for instance because
+			 * access has not been granted yet. Forget it, so that a
+			 * later "change" event can add it.
+			 */
+			devices_.erase(devnum);
 			return -ENODEV;
+		}
 
 		DependencyMap deps;
 		int ret = populateMediaDevice(media.get(), &deps);
@@ -367,7 +374,12 @@
 	LOG(DeviceEnumerator, Debug)
 		<< action << " device " << udev_device_get_devnode(dev);
 
-	if (action == "add")
+	/*
+	 * Access to a device can be granted after it was added: when the
+	 * active session of a seat changes, its devices get a "change" event
+	 * with the new permissions. Devices already known are not added twice.
+	 */
+	if (action == "add" || action == "change")
 		addUdevDevice(dev);
 	else if (action == "remove")
 		removeUdevDevice(dev);
